A||N||5||RiceBurner515||engine swap ||||3||
Z||000000||RiceBurner515||11-10-2000||11:34 AM||||I know there are many reply's on engine swaps and what not that fiero owners can do. I have a 85SE 4cyl. manual, can anybody tell me what engines i could swap with this...i only want to go up to a V6, or i can stay with a L4, doesn't matter...so what engines can i do (4cyl's and V6's)?||||reg||3
Z||000001||Will||11-10-2000||03:39 PM||||What does GM make? Litterally anything smaller than a BBC will fit in a Fiero.<BR>    L4: Quad 4, SD4, Twin-Cam 4, various marine engines<BR>    V6: 2.8, 3.1, 3.2, 3.4 pushrod, 3.4 TDC, 3.5 DOHC (don't know if one of these has been done yet), 3.6 overbore, 3.8, 3.8 S/C, 4.3, 4.3 S/C (don't think one of these has ever been done either)<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Black88GT||11-10-2000||09:11 PM||||What cars have the 3.5 DOHC?  What type of Hp numbers does it produce?<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR> <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Will||11-10-2000||11:17 PM||||The 3.5 DOHC is a very new engine. It was basically made by chopping two cylinders off a Northstar... hence the nickname "Shortstar".<BR>It's used in a few Oldmobiles.<BR>Check out <A HREF="http://www.gmpowertrain.com/engines_cartruck/other/35_main.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.gmpowertrain.com/engines_cartruck/other/35_main.htm</A> <BR>for more info.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Standard||11-11-2000||02:31 AM||||You can put a big block in there, if you don't mind losing your trunk  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 151,000 miles and counting!         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">      <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/asthanos.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||rockcrawl||11-11-2000||06:29 PM||||You can put a big block in there without losing the trunk! Gary Zumalt used to sell a kit to do it for $100 more than his small block kit. Too much weight!<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)||||reg||1
